00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:37.880
Released in 1999, directed by David Fincher, and adapted from the novel by Chuck Pollinick,

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:44.880
Fight Club is an ultraviolent reflection on masculinity, media, corporate culture, gender relationships, self-identity, fatherhood,

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.800
and the conflict between individualism and collectivism.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:55.560
Fight Club, intentionally or not, exposes the crisis of masculine identity as the 'hetero-white-male is displaced' as the societal default,

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:59.180
and the ugly, hazardous reactions to that loss of unquestioned power.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:03.240
As we go through Fight Club, I want to hone the focus to how men interact with each other

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.800
and with the concept of what it means to be a man, the societal construct, the

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:12.500
collective idea that pops into everyone's head when we think of a "real man."

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:19.940
Also, from here on out, when I refer to 'Fight Club' I am, more often than not, referring to the organization within the movie, and not the movie itself.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.560
The first thing that we need to get on the table is the notion of toxic masculinity.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:30.600
The common misinterpretation of this phrase is that it's being used to condemn all masculinity,

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.020
as though manhood itself is something inherently bad,

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.880
Well, this is not true.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:41.020
Toxic masculinity refers to things that are typically encoded as positive or natural masculine traits that are -

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:42.540
under a more critical look -

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.060
actually damaging to self and surrounding.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.320
For example:

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:49.320
"Why? I don't know why. I don't know - never been in a fight. You?"

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.600
"No, but that-that's a good thing."

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.260
"No it is not. How much can you know about yourself if you've never been in a fight?"

00:01:53.900 --> 00:02:03.000
Toxic masculinity is a social script, that tells men and boys that the right way to be a man is to be violent, emotionally unavailable, sexually agressive and soforth.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:08.300
It's a narrow, confining definition of a man that shuts off a vast range of human experiences

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:11.960
and marginalizes the men who fail to conform to that societal standard.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:15.660
It tells them what pursuits are worthy, what styles are acceptable.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:17.500
How a man walks, talks and looks -

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:22.700
Society is structured to reward men who follow the script, and marginalizes those who don't.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:26.720
For example, aggression and hostility are held up as macho standards-

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:33.360
natural, if not desirable traits for men to have, despite their overwhelmingly negative impact on people, groups and society.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:35.860
This has two operative effects:

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.460
First, in lionizing and rewarding aggression,

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.380
and second, in diminishing passivity.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:44.980
For an incredibly real example of the damage that lionizing aggression can cause,

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.620
look no further than investment banking, an industry that attracts and rewards aggression like no other.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:57.200
Passive manner, depicted as lesser, as weaker, as compromised, fake men victimized by society,

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:00.860
and the path to self-acceptance is through the primal embrace of violence.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.100
Take for example, the priest who is recruited into Fight Club.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.200
Yeah! Yeah!
[other men cheer]

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:10.760
Or, in my own life, when discussing this episode's writing on Twitter,

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:15.580
Adam Baldwin sent me this image of macho-Putin punching jet fighters out of the air,

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:20.120
contrasted against what I can only assume is a weak-huggy-feeling Obama.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:25.500
Attached was the message, "Toxic masculinity greater than hashtag New Castrati."

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:31.660
So, this is kindof why this is proven to be such a deep-seated issue in society.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:38.780
The people most invested in the macho identity are actively, knowingly promoting it, and defending it from change or criticism.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:44.160
This narrow masculine script is often presented as naturalistic, or a "biotruth."

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:48.380
Something that's an emergent property of biology and thus immune to criticism.

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.360
The examples of this are long and many:

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.480
"Boys will be boys,"

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:54.580
"Men think about sex every 7 seconds"

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:58.620
"Men can't be friends with women because every man wants to have sex with every woman"

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:03.180
The idea that a "real man" is prepared and willing to get violent at a moments notice,

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.040
And so on and so on and so on.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:11.360
Now, to be clear here, the problem is not in 'being sexual' or being sexually forward,

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:17.280
No one is saying that men should become celibate monks, only donating sperm as needed to perpetuate the species,

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:24.680
The problem is believing that male sexuality is inherently forward and that men are, by nature, unstoppable sex fiends

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:29.780
Not only is this limiting of men, who, say, aren't all that interested in sex,

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:33.620
or who prefer to take a more passive role in their sexual encounters,

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:39.620
It also creates an environment of entitlement, by imbuing sexual aggression with a sort of inevitability.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:44.380
Ideas like "Men can't be friends with women, because he will inevitably try to have sex with her."

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:48.620
Or far worse ideas that trot dubiously along the boundaries of consent.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:54.260
This then cuts both ways, demonizing men as rapists-in-training, such as we saw in 'She's Out of Control."

